    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Mistral3 text and Pixtral image components",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Mistral3Config maps text to Mistral3Model and vision to Mistral3VisionModel. Existing Config.from_directory dispatches through the newly extended registry; Model.from_config selects the requested component, defaulting to text. Text tensors use the language_model. prefix and an embedding \u2192 RMS-normalized attention/SiLU-gated-MLP blocks \u2192 RMSNorm \u2192 logits projection pipeline.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_900f9b083ed742df9f6596fdcb86add8",
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29",
              "call_f03a68ac347b4a488403ee79f832bbb0",
              "call_4dafbcf1e73f4762a3226152a4c9cbd4",
              "call_531e028617cd4572a2e0fbdd300756ee"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Individually, mistralai/Mistral-Small-3.1-24B-Base-2503 and mistralai/Mistral-Small-3.1-24B-Instruct-2503 specify the registered architecture and identical relevant dimensions: text width 5120, 40 layers, head dimension 128, 32 query heads, 8 KV heads, intermediate width 32768 and vocabulary 131072; vision width 1024, 24 layers, head dimension 64, 16 heads, intermediate width 4096 and patch side 14. Both specify merge size 2, three channels, final-layer features and no projector bias. Both omit vision KV-head count, so the adapter defaults it to 16; both omit text tying, so it defaults to false.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_54232fc7e3db4e4daec08c4223fc08a1",
              "call_b486662162e148e9bf1494376431429c",
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Preprocessing composites transparency onto white, converts to RGB, and chooses dimensions aligned to patch_size \u00d7 spatial_merge_size. This prepares complete merge neighborhoods, rather than merely complete convolution patches. It then rescales float32 pixels, applies channel normalization, transposes to channels-first and returns a singleton-batch FP16 tensor. The helper asserts that the maximum dimensions are divisible by that alignment quantum; it does not provide a final maximum-size clamp.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29",
              "call_0035c45b902448e4b3b28252bf05770f",
              "call_6c79721059194cfca1c96eb08b067701",
              "call_ff34699dcb8445a19f8865da2111e459"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The vision tower uses patch-strided Conv, pre-RMSNorm and 24 configured transformer blocks with RMSNorm, rotary attention and SiLU-gated MLPs. Conv flattens its spatial result into row-major tokens. The vision MLPs request pad_to=1, preserving exact dimensions. get_image_embeddings supplies causal=False and no cache; Attention consequently defaults to its no-cache FlashAttention route. The existing SDPA alternative rejects sliding windows and softcaps, neither of which this tower configures.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29",
              "call_f12d287918294e5a9bda518ab78ac214",
              "call_531e028617cd4572a2e0fbdd300756ee",
              "call_2c6322bba0b744bb8f74173efb9b4a4d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The vision constructor builds a two-dimensional RoPE angle table: alternating entries of the ordinary inverse-frequency sequence go to height and width, then their outer products are concatenated. For maximum patch-grid side N, token (row,column) selects table row row\u00d7N+column. Attention transfers the supplied table to its device and RoPE.apply forwards it to CUDA, where table entries are angles evaluated with sine/cosine, not frequencies multiplied by position again. The tower constructs its actual RopeSettings directly from vision head dimension and theta; the separately parsed vision.rope_settings object is not used by that constructor.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29",
              "call_2c6322bba0b744bb8f74173efb9b4a4d",
              "call_adc22881a5fd439ca23f194d9c7ee194",
              "call_36539a2c2a5d44d4a63f2dc53dae6b66"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "After projector RMSNorm, Mistral3PatchMerger requires batch size one and features_size=(height,width). It reshapes the sequence into a spatial grid, unfolds nonoverlapping merge\u00d7merge neighborhoods, and projects hidden_size\u00d7merge\u00b2 back to hidden_size. An ordinary GELU MLP then maps vision width through a hardcoded 5120 intermediate to text width. The existing MLP out_size feature supplies the unequal endpoint widths; its GELU implementation uses the tanh approximation. The 5120 specialization agrees with the inspected Base projector tensors rather than being a general configuration-derived width.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29",
              "call_531e028617cd4572a2e0fbdd300756ee",
              "call_d88f92a99e054b67b42e5f91bd823b19"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The Base shard headers contain every requested primary weight across text layers 0\u201339 and vision layers 0\u201323. Text Q is [4096,5120], K/V [1024,5120], O [5120,4096], gate/up [32768,5120], down [5120,32768], with [5120] norms and [131072,5120] embedding/head weights. Vision attention matrices are [1024,1024], gate/up [4096,1024], down [1024,4096], norms [1024], and patch convolution [1024,3,14,14]. Projector merger, linear_1 and linear_2 weights are respectively [1024,4096], [5120,1024] and [5120,5120]. These stored output-by-input linear shapes agree with Linear's default transposed loading.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d88f92a99e054b67b42e5f91bd823b19",
              "call_3972d2bf561d43b888ee58f3c6672bd9",
              "call_072876b4831c4c99b4bc329a5c7db2b2",
              "call_66e339f7f4794bb593fbb446f38625d9",
              "call_fb02e115b28e402f856bae31e7546c5f",
              "call_fe86553ce34a4fccaf735ea5bdf43b51",
              "call_ea96fae4364240079d3674dd5bbcce2e",
              "call_2276c688701f4d9cb484f8dd6e1270d7",
              "call_9251c6db5c204782bb171f90cc6887d8",
              "call_c122c927a48541e4a1e267bcd984fdb9",
              "call_c9aa688c05cd45479dee680046d09c36"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Those Base headers contain weights only: optional convolution/linear biases and linear weight_scale_inv tensors are absent, so their loaders take the no-bias/no-FP8-scale path. EXL3 storage groups are absent, selecting ordinary weight loading. The untied language head exists, so no embedding fallback is needed. No stored weight in the inspected Hugging Face-format shards is left without a corresponding component module.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d88f92a99e054b67b42e5f91bd823b19",
              "call_3972d2bf561d43b888ee58f3c6672bd9",
              "call_072876b4831c4c99b4bc329a5c7db2b2",
              "call_66e339f7f4794bb593fbb446f38625d9",
              "call_fb02e115b28e402f856bae31e7546c5f",
              "call_fe86553ce34a4fccaf735ea5bdf43b51",
              "call_ea96fae4364240079d3674dd5bbcce2e",
              "call_2276c688701f4d9cb484f8dd6e1270d7",
              "call_9251c6db5c204782bb171f90cc6887d8",
              "call_c122c927a48541e4a1e267bcd984fdb9",
              "call_c9aa688c05cd45479dee680046d09c36",
              "call_f12d287918294e5a9bda518ab78ac214",
              "call_8c4c05a47fb3480f9560492a160bd6e4",
              "call_2a7b3ffc387446f8b161ed80984d4e3e",
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "get_image_embeddings moves projected vectors to CPU and constructs one -1 placeholder per merged patch, an [IMG_BREAK] after each row, then [IMG_END]. MMEmbedding replaces placeholders with synthetic token IDs while retaining the vectors and alias. This agrees with the existing container interface and Embedding's indexed-vector reader. The parent has one other MMEmbedding builder, Gemma3, which instead surrounds its placeholders with start/end image IDs. The existing multimodal example uses this interface but remains configured for Gemma3; the task adds no Mistral3 prompt example.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29",
              "call_8367c490480c4f9b864f6d5ef785e847",
              "call_935cd1bc887f49ffb270f723ab6fda09",
              "call_2a7b3ffc387446f8b161ed80984d4e3e",
              "call_837ef18a54354c309262e3373987250d",
              "call_0092066ba32448afa8b3cf1bd73238f3",
              "call_4f8e1f7022b34e32b56cd621ce3bf576"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library arithmetic transcription, conditional on preprocessor longest_edge=1540, gives a 110\u00d7110 patch grid, a [12100,32] angle table, merger input width 4096, and 55\u00d755=3025 image vectors serialized into 3081 tokens. It also checks rectangular row\u00d7N+column indexing without aliasing inside the valid grid. These are shape/index calculations, not tensor or model execution.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e12d0a063ac5492a81225a19678ba15f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Autosplit now creates one params dictionary from default_load_params and shares it through module device preparation and forward calls, instead of passing fresh empty dictionaries. Mistral3VisionModel supplies the maximum feature-grid dimensions needed by its merger; the base hook returns {}. Whole-parent searches found no existing hook collision, only the base/Gemma3 load-shape implementations, and only load_gen calling _load_autosplit. Gemma3 remains on the empty-parameter default. Explicit single-device loading does not run this probe.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c8f51d5b633a4059b2309453ce7e1d93",
              "call_3e30be17b6284c9b95e8ae7daa523b29",
              "call_70d824adf82d42618e2d5d257bd88663",
              "call_2203c455a2f44daa8c817bd1e57d7c12",
              "call_03354cd65ce94ab192cd836a9faa1fbc",
              "call_869de16301f34a0fb1c2868a58168a27",
              "call_4dafbcf1e73f4762a3226152a4c9cbd4",
              "call_837ef18a54354c309262e3373987250d"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "resize-overflow-reaches-vision-rope-table",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The new image pipeline inherits an unclamped floating-point resize overflow, allowing feature positions outside its precomputed RoPE table.",
        "trigger": "Use an otherwise valid processor configuration with longest_edge=1540, patch_size=14 and spatial_merge_size=2, then call Mistral3VisionModel.get_image_embeddings with a 28\u00d71541 image.",
        "expected_behavior": "Resize to merge-aligned dimensions within the configured maximum, keeping every generated position ID inside the angle table.",
        "actual_behavior": "The scalar transcription rounds the limiting height to 1541 before alignment and returns 28\u00d71568. The new caller therefore builds features_size=(112,2), with position IDs reaching 12211 despite only 12100 table rows. Neither the image caller nor the inspected CUDA wrapper validates row bounds. Source reach is the new get_image_embeddings \u2192 preprocess \u2192 helper \u2192 vision attention path; the parent had no caller of the sizing helper. No resulting image-library behavior or GPU fault was observed.",
        "locations": [
          {
            "commit": "45fa5abff9001ff373a612303e48ec01d34efe42",
            "path": "exllamav3/models/mistral3.py",
            "symbol": "Mistral3VisionModel.preprocess / get_image_embeddings"
          },
          {
            "commit": "45fa5abff9001ff373a612303e48ec01d34efe42",
            "path": "exllamav3/util/vision.py",
            "symbol": "size_to_longest_edge_and_patch_size"
          }
        ],
        "source_evidence": [
